{
  "name": "topo_pen_surface_raycast",
  "description": "Topology Pen P0/P2 (doc/topopen_p0_plan.md, doc/topopen_p2_plan.md): the CONS stage's background-surface constraint, probed through GET /api/surface-raycast. The original P0 cases all exercise `geometry screen` (camera-ray -- the CENTRE pixel's ray passes through the camera's `focus` point EXACTLY, a property of the lookAt-based camera construction, independent of azimuth/elevation/distance, so a case sets `focus` to the exact world point it wants the ray to land on); they were authored under a `geometry point` argstring back when P0's raycast branch was gated on Point but ALWAYS did a camera-ray search regardless of mode -- P2c corrected a mode bug: for an over-surface CLICK, Point mode places at the SAME camera-ray/surface hit as Screen (the tool's seed IS the ray-hit, already on the surface, so the nearest-foot refinement is a no-op), so these camera-ray cases are relabeled `geometry screen` (unchanged values -- honest, every one genuinely exercises a camera ray). The `point_*` cases exercise Point mode and assert it produces IDENTICAL output to Screen for the same camera+pixel (Point == Screen for a click; they use a Screen-mirroring camera). All expected numbers are hand-derived analytically (fan-triangle cross products, point-to-segment distances, ray/surface intersection) and cross-checked with an independent Python re-implementation of screenRay/lookAt/sphericalToCartesian; no reference 3D modeling tool's output was used.",
  "provenance": {
    "schema": 1,
    "source": "analytic",
    "reference": "analytic",
    "method": "closed-form",
    "captured_utc": "unknown",
    "harness": null,
    "task": "topopen-p0-p2",
    "notes": "Hand-authored fixture for the topology-pen P0 background-surface-raycast plumbing (doc/topopen_p0_plan.md) and P2's Point-mode nearest-foot correction (doc/topopen_p2_plan.md). Every camera-ray (`screen`) case's hit point/normal/nearestVert/nearestEdge is derived analytically from the loaded mesh's own vertex coordinates (fan-triangle normals, point-to-segment closest-point) and the camera's guaranteed centre-pixel-through-focus property; cross-checked against a standalone Python replica of math.d's screenRay/lookAt/sphericalToCartesian (not committed) to bound the sub-pixel sampling error at <=0.016 world units for every case, comfortably inside the suite's 0.02 tolerance. 'bg_cube_bottom_face' stands in for the plan's 'bg_sphere_center' case -- hand-authoring an exact UV-sphere fixture (face indices + tangent-plane normals) was not practical without generator tooling; a third distinct cube face (-Y, previously untested by the top/+X/-X cases) exercises the same normal-direction diversity goal. 'bg_quad_tilted_normal' (review NIT-4) is 'bg_quad_offcenter' rotated 30deg about world X -- every other case's background face is axis-aligned, so this is the only case whose expected normal has all three components nonzero, exercising pickSurfaceRay's cross(b-a,c-a) fan-triangle normal against a genuinely oblique FACE (not just an oblique camera ray). The `point_*` cases (P2) each pick a camera dominant along ONE world axis (Y for the +X/-Z faces, X for the -Y face, via `mostFacingAxis`'s abs-dot argmax over the camera's back vector) so the auto work-plane's normal is that axis and its plane passes through the world origin (WorkplaneStage's auto-mode publish); `focus`'s component along that SAME axis is set to exactly 0 so the work-plane-cursor seed coincides with `focus` (mirrors the screen-mode trick, just against the work-plane instead of the mesh) -- the other two `focus` components are chosen so exactly one of them exceeds the unit cube's +-0.5 half-extent, making the expected nearest-foot a simple per-axis clamp of `focus` against the box, landing on a specific face/normal with no tie (each case's excess axis is >=1.5 units past the boundary, comfortably outside any float/BVH-adjacent tie region)."
  },
  "tolerance": 0.02,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "bg_cube_topface_center",
      "input": [
        { "reset": true },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain enabled true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain geometry screen" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.add name:Bg" },
        { "endpoint": "load-mesh", "body": {
            "vertices": [[-0.5,-0.5,-0.5],[0.5,-0.5,-0.5],[0.5,0.5,-0.5],[-0.5,0.5,-0.5],
                         [-0.5,-0.5,0.5],[0.5,-0.5,0.5],[0.5,0.5,0.5],[-0.5,0.5,0.5]],
            "faces": [[0,3,2,1],[4,5,6,7],[0,4,7,3],[1,2,6,5],[3,7,6,2],[0,1,5,4]]
          } },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.setVisible index:1 value:true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.select index:0" },
        { "endpoint": "camera", "body": {
            "azimuth": 0.4, "elevation": 0.6, "distance": 4,
            "focus": {"x": 0, "y": 0.5, "z": 0}
          } }
      ],
      "raycast": { "x": 475, "y": 300 },
      "expected": {
        "hit": true, "layer": 1, "face": 4,
        "point": [0, 0.5, 0], "normal": [0, 1, 0]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "bg_quad_offcenter",
      "input": [
        { "reset": true },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain enabled true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "tool.pipe.attr constrain geometry screen" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.add name:Bg" },
        { "endpoint": "load-mesh", "body": {
            "vertices": [[-10,0,-10],[10,0,-10],[10,0,10],[-10,0,10]],
            "faces": [[0,2,1],[0,3,2]]
          } },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.setVisible index:1 value:true" },
        { "endpoint": "command", "argstring": "layer.select index:0" },
        { "endpoint": "camera", "body": {
            "azimuth": 0.35, "elevation": 0.87, "distance": 6,
